ategory><category>bernoulli-map</category><category>probabilistic-data-structures</category><category>hashing</category><category>information-theory</category><category>bernoulli-model</category></item><item><title>A Boolean Algebra Over Trapdoors</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/trapdoor-boolean-model/</link><pubDate>Sat, 17 Jun 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/trapdoor-boolean-model/</guid><description>A Boolean algebra framework over trapdoors for cryptographic operations. Introduces a homomorphism from powerset Boolean algebra to n-bit strings via cryptographic hash functions, enabling secure computations with one-way properties.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/trapdoor-boolean-model/featured.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Probabilistic Data Structures</media:title></media:content><category>cryptography</category><category>boolean-algebra</category><category>probabilistic-data-structures</category><category>bernoulli-model</category></item><item><title>Noisy Turing Machines: Noisy Logic Gates</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2023-06-17-noisy-gates/</link><pubDate>Sat, 17 Jun 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2023-06-17-noisy-gates/</guid><description>Analyzing how Bernoulli Boolean types propagate through logic circuits, with correctness probabilities for noisy AND gates and interval arithmetic for composed circuits.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2023-06-17-noisy-gates/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Probabilistic Data Structures</media:title></media:content><category>probabilistic-data-structures</category><category>probability</category><category>type-theory</category><category>computation</category><category>bernoulli-model</category></item><item><title>The Bernoulli Model: A Probabilistic Framework for Data Structures and Types</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/bernoulli-boolean-model/</link><pubDate>Sat, 17 Jun 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/bernoulli-boolean-model/</guid><description>The Bernoulli Model is a framework for reasoning about probabilistic data structures by treating noisy outputs as Bernoulli-distributed approximations of latent values, from Booleans to set-indicator functions.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/bernoulli-boolean-model/featured.png" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Probabilistic Data Structures</media:title></media:content><category>probabilistic-data-structures</category><category>bloom-filter</category><category>probability</category><category>type-theory</category><category>bernoulli-model</category></item><item><title>Boolean Algebra over Trapdoor Sets: A Practical Framework for Privacy-Preserving Set Operations with Probabilistic Guarantees</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/papers/boolean-algebra-trapdoor-sets/</link><pubDate>Sat, 01 Jan 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/papers/boolean-algebra-trapdoor-sets/</guid><description> Open full page Download PDF</description><category>oblivious computing</category><category>hash-based sets</category><category>privacy-preserving</category><category>set operations</category><category>probabilistic data structures</category><category>Bloom filters</category><category>cryptographic hashing</category><category>encrypted search</category><category>oblivious data structures</category><category>trapdoor sets</category></item><item><title>Bloom Filters</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2015-03-bloom-filters/</link><pubDate>Sun, 15 Mar 2015 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink